---
import LandingLayout from '../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';
import ProductBlock from '../components/ProductBlock.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
import { page } from '../data/site';
const related = [page('/home-inventory-app/'), page('/new-homeowner-app/'), page('/digital-home-binder/')];
// The paint screenshots are 921x2000 iPhone captures.
const shot = { width: 921, height: 2000 };
---
<LandingLayout
  title="Paint Color Tracker for Your Home | Around The House"
  description="Remember the paint color, code, brand, finish, and room for your next touch-up. For iPhone, iPad, and Mac."
  canonicalPath="/paint-color-tracker/"
  breadcrumbLabel="Paint color tracker"
  h1="Remember exactly which paint you used."
  intro="The label on the can in the garage is half peeled off, and the receipt went out with the recycling. Around The House keeps the color name, code, brand, and finish with the room it went on, so the next touch-up starts with the details instead of a guess."
  ctaHeading="Start with the room you painted last."
  ctaBody="It's the one you still have the can for."
>
  <figure slot="hero-media" class="product-block-shot">
    <img
      src="/assets/screenshots/new/iphone-paint-record.webp"
      width={shot.width}
      height={shot.height}
      alt="Example exterior paint record in Around The House on iPhone: Oakwood Meadow by Harborline, color code HL-7420, Satin finish, used on the whole exterior's fiber cement siding, with an approximate color preview, a Copy Paint Details button, a photo labeled Paint Can, and the product line, base, and tint formula."
      fetchpriority="high"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </figure>

  <section>
    <h2>What a paint record holds</h2>
    <p>The top of a paint record answers the question you have at the paint counter. The screenshot above is an example exterior paint, Oakwood Meadow.</p>
    <ul class="qa-list">
      <li><strong>Color name, brand, and code</strong><span>The name is how you recognize it. The code, with the brand that made it, is what the paint counter needs to mix it again.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Finish</strong><span>Flat, eggshell, satin, semi-gloss. The same color in a different sheen won't look the same on the wall.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Where it's used</strong><span>The area and surface, such as the whole exterior on fiber cement siding, shown right under the name.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Product line, base, and tint formula</strong><span>The details printed on the store's mixing label. With the formula, a store can tint the same base the same way.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Photos</strong><span>A picture of the can or its label, with a label of its own, such as Paint Can, so you know what each photo shows.</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p>The swatch is marked as an approximate color preview. A screen can't show true paint color, so use it to recognize the record, not to match the paint.</p>
    <p>Copy Paint Details copies the record's details so you can paste them where you need them, like a message to a painter or a note for the store.</p>
  </section>

  <ProductBlock src="/assets/screenshots/new/iphone-paint-purchase-application.webp" width={shot.width} height={shot.height} alt="Middle of the same example paint record on iPhone. Where It's Used lists Whole Exterior, Fiber cement siding, painted Jun 17, 2023, with Add Another Location. Purchase shows Dockside Paint &amp; Supply, purchased Jun 9, 2023, $389.00, 5 gallons, and about 1 gallon left on the garage shelf. Application shows 2 coats, spot-primed bare boards, painted by ProCoat Painters.">
    <h2>Where it went and what it took</h2>
    <p>One paint can cover more than one place. Each location keeps its own area, surface, and painted date, and you can add another when the same color goes on a second room.</p>
    <p>The purchase section keeps the store, date, price, and quantity, plus how much is left and where it is, like "about 1 gallon, garage shelf."</p>
    <p>The application section records when it was painted, how many coats, the primer, and who did the work, so the next job can start from what worked last time.</p>
  </ProductBlock>

  <ProductBlock flip src="/assets/screenshots/new/iphone-paint-history-documents.webp" width={shot.width} height={shot.height} alt="Lower part of the same example paint record on iPhone. Touch-Up Notes say body, trim, and front door colors are recorded so touch-ups match without guessing. Paint History lists Touched up front door trim on Jun 21, 2026, with Log Paint Work. Documents holds an exterior paint receipt PDF, with Add Document and a note that document attachments are included with Around the House Pro. More offers Add Reminder.">
    <h2>Touch-ups, history, and the receipt</h2>
    <p>Touch-up notes hold the advice you'd give yourself, like which colors go on the body, trim, and front door.</p>
    <p>Each touch-up or repaint can be logged as paint work, so the record shows what was done and when. The receipt can sit with the paint it paid for. Document attachments are part of Around The House Pro.</p>
    <p>You can also add a reminder from the same record, for a recoat or a seasonal check.</p>
  </ProductBlock>

  <section>
    <h2>When a wall gets scuffed</h2>
    <p>A dragged chair leaves a mark in the dining room, or a picture comes down and leaves nail holes to patch. You open the room's paint record and read off the brand, code, and finish instead of hunting for the can.</p>
    <p>Having the exact code gets you the same color formula, but it can't promise an invisible repair. Older paint on the wall fades, and sheen and application change how a patch looks. For anything bigger than a small spot, painting to the nearest corner usually blends better.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Kept with the rest of the house</h2>
    <p>Paint records live in Around The House alongside your appliances, repairs, and documents, on iPhone, iPad, and Mac, without a separate company account. They stay on your devices and, when you turn it on, in your private iCloud.</p>
  </section>

  <RelatedLinks heading="Related records" items={related} />
</LandingLayout>
